<!-- STRAIGHT ANSWERS -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Straight answers</h2>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Why The Web3 Family?</h3>
        <div>
          <p>Web 1 was pages you read. Web 2 was pages you posted to, and somebody else kept what you made. Web 3 is a newer term for a simple idea: what you make belongs to you.</p>
          <p>That idea is the whole reason for the name. Family is the plain part. You get one person who knows your work and stays with it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What happens if I stop?</h3>
        <p>You keep all of it. Every file, every account, every password, already in your organization’s name.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What do you need from me?</h3>
        <p>Two hours a week and your honest opinion. You talk. Friday you look over what came out and tell me what to fix.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Where does all of this end up?</h3>
        <p>In one place, in order, under your organization’s name. After a year you have everything your organization has said, made, and figured out, and the people who come after you can find it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

